{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And the eye of their Elohim</b> — The verse relates that HaShem helped them, and they did not cease. The final heh in the word אלההום is from להום; in the books [of the Aramaic targumim] it says אלהא דלהום." "<b>יהך</b> — 'go.' Translation [of הלך] as in 'if you walk with me בקרי' (2 Kings 3:14)."], :book :ezra, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {0 "The referent of 'the books' is uncertain; possibly the Aramaic targumim or other Aramaic biblical texts."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Ezra -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:41:59.605430002Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}